Original Zero checks and historical review fixtures

The active verifier is authored in tools/check.zero:
  zero-check PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_TEST_DIRECTORY
Its source fixtures and exact expectations live in checks/. Read the complete
contract with zero-text read checks/README.ztext. The original Zero verifier
loads the owned compiler application, compiles the frontend/packer and runs
language fixtures in process, then performs native host file checks.

The Zero/Ezero programs below review-tests/ are retained review fixtures from
earlier compiler, filesystem, window and boot work. Their old orchestration
scripts and generated result trees were removed. Historical capacity numbers,
exit expectations and prior pass counts must not be treated as current proof.
The active compiler grammar is documented in SYNTAX.ztext and LANGUAGE.ztext.
Native host checks do not replace firmware, disk-restart or hardware tests.
